NODICS SOURCE-AVAILABLE COMMERCIAL LICENSE
Version 1.0
Effective date: 2026-08-02

IMPORTANT NOTICE

This license is intended to describe the commercial and source-available use
model for the Nodics Framework. It is not an open-source license. It contains
commercial, resale, hosted-service, and productization restrictions. If you need
rights that are not expressly granted below, you must obtain a separate written
agreement with Nodics.

This license should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before public
distribution, enforcement, or production partner onboarding.

1. Parties

"Nodics", "we", "us", or "our" means Nodics or the legal entity that owns or
controls the Nodics Framework copyrights, trademarks, and commercial licensing
rights.

"You" or "your" means the individual, company, partner, contractor, affiliate,
or legal entity that accesses, copies, modifies, evaluates, develops with,
deploys, or distributes the Licensed Materials.

2. Licensed Materials

"Licensed Materials" means the Nodics Framework source code, object code,
configuration, schemas, scripts, generated templates, generated artifacts,
documentation, examples, tests, tools, module definitions, BackOffice/Axis
contracts, commerce modules, media modules, workflow/pipeline infrastructure,
and any other materials distributed by Nodics under this license.

"Nodics Framework" means the backend/API framework, runtime, modules, tooling,
schemas, configuration model, extension model, generated assets, and related
framework-owned materials supplied by Nodics.

"Nodics Client Applications" means Nodics-owned or Nodics-supplied user
interfaces, administration clients, BackOffice clients, Axis clients,
documentation clients, storefront clients, or other experience applications
distributed with or for the Nodics Framework.

3. Ownership

Nodics and its licensors retain all right, title, and interest in and to the
Licensed Materials, including all copyrights, patent rights, trade secret
rights, trademark rights, know-how, architecture, module design, schemas,
tooling, documentation, and all other intellectual property rights.

Except for the limited rights expressly granted in this license, no rights are
granted by implication, exhaustion, estoppel, or otherwise.

4. License Type

The Licensed Materials are source-available commercial software. Access to
source code does not make the Licensed Materials open source, public domain,
free software, or unrestricted software.

You may not describe the Licensed Materials as open source unless Nodics
separately publishes an OSI-approved open-source license for the applicable
materials.

5. Definitions

"Application" means software, services, modules, integrations, extensions,
business processes, commerce journeys, operational workflows, customer
experiences, or business solutions built using, extending, embedding, deploying,
or integrating with the Licensed Materials.

"Internal Use" means use of the Licensed Materials by you solely to develop,
test, deploy, operate, support, or maintain Applications for your own internal
business operations, not for resale, white-labeling, multi-customer commercial
offering, or commercial product distribution.

"Customer-Specific Application" means an Application built by a partner,
contractor, system integrator, agency, or service provider for one identified
end customer, where the Application is customized for that customer's own
internal business operations and is not marketed, licensed, sublicensed, sold,
or offered as a reusable product to multiple customers.

"Commercial Product" means any Application, platform, product, package,
template, marketplace offering, managed service, hosted service, SaaS offering,
PaaS offering, framework, SDK, accelerator, starter kit, white-label solution,
or repeatable commercial solution that is built on, embeds, includes,
distributes, exposes, substantially depends on, competes with, or is derived
from the Licensed Materials and is offered to third parties for sale, license,
subscription, hosting, resale, outsourcing, or other commercial exploitation.

"Resale" means selling, licensing, sublicensing, distributing, white-labeling,
packaging, hosting, monetizing, transferring, or commercially offering an
Application or Commercial Product to third parties in a manner that is not
limited to one Customer-Specific Application.

"Hosted Service" or "Managed Service" means providing third parties with access
to the functionality, APIs, administration capabilities, runtime behavior,
schema workbench, media management, commerce capabilities, workflow/pipeline
capabilities, generated applications, or substantial features of the Licensed
Materials through a hosted, managed, cloud, SaaS, PaaS, subscription,
outsourcing, or service-provider model.

"Partner" means any person or entity that develops, configures, integrates,
customizes, deploys, operates, supports, or maintains Applications using the
Licensed Materials for itself or for an end customer.

"End Customer" means the specific company, organization, or legal entity for
whose own internal business operations a Customer-Specific Application is
developed, deployed, or operated.

"Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common
control with a party, where control means ownership or control of more than 50%
of the voting interests or the practical power to direct management decisions.

"Contractor" means a third party acting on your behalf and under your control
to perform development, implementation, testing, deployment, operation,
maintenance, or support of an approved Application.

"Customer Module" or "Extension Module" means a project-specific module,
adapter, configuration layer, schema extension, service override, renderer,
workflow, pipeline action, or integration created to customize the Licensed
Materials without modifying framework-owned source code.

"Support Contract" means a separate written commercial agreement with Nodics
that grants commercial support, partner rights, resale rights, productization
rights, managed-service rights, hosted-service rights, production certification,
or other rights not granted by this license.

6. Permitted Use Without Separate Commercial Resale Rights

Subject to your compliance with this license, Nodics grants you a limited,
non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable license to:

a. access and review the Licensed Materials;
b. copy the Licensed Materials for evaluation, development, testing, staging,
   demonstration, and approved production operation;
c. modify the Licensed Materials or create Customer Modules solely for Internal
   Use or Customer-Specific Applications;
d. develop, deploy, operate, maintain, and support Applications for Internal
   Use;
e. develop, deploy, operate, maintain, and support Customer-Specific
   Applications for one identified End Customer;
f. allow your employees, Affiliates, and Contractors to access the Licensed
   Materials only as necessary for the permitted use and only if they are bound
   by confidentiality, security, and license restrictions at least as protective
   as this license;
g. run the Licensed Materials in private, customer-controlled, on-premises,
   private cloud, or approved public cloud environments for permitted use; and
h. create backups, disaster-recovery copies, and internal deployment artifacts
   reasonably necessary for permitted use.

7. Uses Requiring a Separate Nodics Commercial or Support Contract

You must obtain a separate written Support Contract or commercial license from
Nodics before you, directly or indirectly:

a. sell, license, sublicense, distribute, rent, lease, resell, white-label, or
   commercially offer a Commercial Product built on or containing the Licensed
   Materials;
b. offer a hosted, managed, SaaS, PaaS, marketplace, app-builder, low-code,
   no-code, framework, SDK, integration platform, or service-provider offering
   that exposes or substantially uses the Licensed Materials;
c. build a repeatable product or accelerator for multiple customers using the
   Licensed Materials;
d. provide a multi-tenant or multi-customer commercial service based on the
   Licensed Materials;
e. embed the Licensed Materials in a packaged commercial product, appliance,
   downloadable product, marketplace app, or white-label solution;
f. provide paid support, managed operations, certification, warranty, or
   maintenance for the Licensed Materials as an independent commercial offering;
g. use the Licensed Materials to create, operate, or commercialize a framework,
   platform, product, or service that competes with Nodics;
h. remove, obscure, bypass, alter, or disable license, attribution, governance,
   security, audit, entitlement, telemetry, or usage-control mechanisms;
i. use the Licensed Materials for benchmarking, public competitive analysis, or
   marketing comparisons without Nodics' prior written consent; or
j. exercise any right not expressly granted in this license.

8. Prohibited Conduct

You must not:

a. use the Licensed Materials outside the scope of this license;
b. disclose source code or confidential implementation details except as
   permitted by this license or a written agreement with Nodics;
c. remove, alter, or obscure copyright, license, trademark, confidentiality,
   attribution, security, or ownership notices;
d. use Nodics trademarks, logos, product names, service names, or branding in a
   way that suggests endorsement, partnership, certification, or sponsorship
   without written permission;
e. reverse engineer, decompile, or circumvent any component provided only in
   object-code form except to the extent applicable law prohibits this
   restriction;
f. bypass or weaken security, authentication, authorization, tenant isolation,
   license, entitlement, audit, observability, or governance controls;
g. use the Licensed Materials to violate law, infringe rights, compromise
   systems, misappropriate data, or process regulated data without required
   controls;
h. publish secrets, credentials, customer data, tenant data, private paths,
   private runtime configuration, or security-sensitive diagnostics; or
i. grant any third party rights broader than the rights you receive under this
   license.

9. Customer-Specific Implementations

A Partner may build and deliver a Customer-Specific Application for an End
Customer without separate resale rights only if:

a. the Application is for one identified End Customer;
b. the Application is not marketed or reused as a Commercial Product;
c. the End Customer uses the Application for its own internal business
   operations;
d. the Partner does not offer the Application as a hosted multi-customer or
   white-label service unless separately authorized;
e. all source access, deployment access, and operational access remains subject
   to confidentiality and this license; and
f. Nodics copyright, license, and attribution notices are preserved.

If the same or substantially similar Application is packaged, marketed,
licensed, hosted, sold, or reused for multiple customers, it is treated as a
Commercial Product and requires a separate Nodics commercial agreement.

10. Customer Modules and Ownership of Your Work

Subject to Nodics' ownership of the Licensed Materials, you own your original
Customer Modules, business data, customer-specific configuration, authored
content, custom integrations, and application-specific code that you create
independently and that does not copy or modify Nodics-owned source code.

Your ownership does not give you the right to commercialize, resell, host,
white-label, distribute, or productize the Licensed Materials except as allowed
by this license or a separate written agreement.

If your Customer Module modifies, copies, or includes Nodics-owned source code,
that portion remains subject to this license.

11. Contributions and Feedback

Unless a separate written contribution agreement says otherwise, if you submit
code, documentation, patches, ideas, issue reports, suggestions, designs,
schemas, examples, or other feedback to Nodics, you grant Nodics a perpetual,
irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, fully paid, sublicensable, transferable
